    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n29577" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mŏnŏdūs</span></b> ,
			ontos, m.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μονόδους</span>, onetoothed,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a son of
				Prusias, who had only a solid bone instead of
			teeth</i>.—So, also, <i>Pyrrhus, king of the
				Epirotæ</i>, Paul. ex <i><span class="en">Fest. p.
				148</span></i> Müll.; cf. <i><span class="en">Plin. 7, 16,
				15, § 69</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Val. Max.
				1, 8, 12</span></i>
			<i>ext.</i></div>
